#{[17592186387978 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387978 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387978 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387978 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=y-x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387978 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e75a1d08-2fa1-51fa-b251-a3f4ae4ef9d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387978 #edb/ref 1074 "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ y-x & =c \\\\ y & =x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/91/91fde8bc9eb57c1974e622a6673a030c9889c77d6788b620ffe70d7d6a8409c5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387979 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8a1b305a-d716-5bd9-a834-19012dc96cc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387980 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c2/c2c7ac29fce22a4448d286307dd3a87839c413f0a422cbdc2dbd13dc04144a7b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387980 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387980 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c206