er only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =c \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $y=-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](images/67/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186387996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387993 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5053c438-eb23-5e9c-bd54-db15189721dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387994 #edb/ref 1080 "images/56/56e923e4c1e2603c9bd3c621df0a5a4043fcc6a37ac73427be14541407fc19d8.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69ffca37-cace-5fde-98f2-279fdf4f3975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387995 #edb/ref 1080 "images/09/09f1a18e1a6fdcd29a40026cbffd8e8bdec23511bb692a1e920c18f942042470.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387995 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186387995 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ef1d420-a12a-56ca